WEBVTT

00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:31.379
We should be envying Ghana,

00:01:31.379 --> 00:01:34.590
Brazil, Turkey, Serbia, Japan,

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.883
the United Kingdom,

00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:39.178
Norway, the Netherlands, Sweden --

00:01:39.178 --> 00:01:42.431
we’re lagging behind the world on this.

00:01:42.473 --> 00:01:44.016
When I say paid family leave,

00:01:44.016 --> 00:01:48.521
I’m not talking about necessarily
just newborn maternity leave.

00:01:48.521 --> 00:01:50.273
That includes paternity leave,

00:01:50.273 --> 00:01:51.274
all genders,

00:01:51.274 --> 00:01:54.527
families that are adopting
and welcoming a new child into their home,

00:01:54.527 --> 00:01:56.779
people bringing foster children
into their home,

00:01:56.779 --> 00:01:58.197
taking care of aging parents.

00:01:58.406 --> 00:02:00.366
You know, at some point in your life,